But considering the nature of the priority queue and the fact that `null` elements are not allowed, we can further simplify it to:

<code>assert \old(this.size()) > 0 && this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), result) <= 0;</code>

If the comparator is `null`, the natural ordering of the elements should be used. Therefore, we need to handle both cases:

<code>assert \old(this.size()) > 0 && ((this.comparator() == null && ((Comparable<? super E>) this.peek()).compareTo(result) <= 0) || (this.comparator() != null && this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), result) <= 0));</code>

This ensures that the new head is no greater than the old head, considering both natural ordering and custom comparator scenarios.

